-- title:
--   Unramified charts commute with the X'-tower transitions
-- statement:
--   The statement is set in the following situation.
--
--   *Base ring.* A prime $r$; a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an irreducible element $\pi \in \mathcal O$, completeness of $\mathcal O$ for the $\pi$-adic topology (`hcomplete`), the requirement that $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ have exactly $r$ elements (`hres`) and that $(r) = (\pi)$ in $\mathcal O$ (`hunr`); a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is the fraction field of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   *Unramified layer.* A characteristic-zero domain $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, together with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $F_r$ of it, subject to: completeness for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), maximality of that ideal (`hOnr_max`), that every element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), that every monic polynomial of positive degree over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and that $F_r(x) \equiv x^r \pmod \pi$ for all $x$ (`hFr`).
--
--   *Valuation of the determinant.* A homomorphism $v_{\det} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by `hvdet`: $v_{\det}(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   *Group data.* A group $G$, a homomorphism $\sigma : G \to \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and a subgroup $\Gamma \le G$; `hcent` asks for some $z \in \Gamma$ with $\sigma z$ a scalar matrix and $v_{\det}(\sigma z) = 2$, and `hodd` for some $w \in \Gamma$ with $v_{\det}(\sigma w) = 1$; a subgroup $\Gamma'$ characterised by `hΓ'` as the set of $x \in \Gamma$ with $v_{\det}(\sigma x)$ even; a homomorphism $\rho : G \to \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ which is the projectivisation of $\sigma$ (`hρ`); discreteness `hdisc`, saying that for every vertex $v$ of the lattice tree [`LT.LatticeTree.Vertex 𝒪 K₀`](def/LatticeTreeOrbital.html#L349) the set of elements of $\rho(\Gamma')$ fixing $v$ is finite; and cocompactness `hcocpt`, asking for a finite set of vertices meeting every $\rho(\Gamma')$-orbit.
--
--   *Mumford tower.* An element $g_1 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ equal to $\operatorname{diag}(\pi,1)$ (`hg₁`); a subgroup $N \le \rho(\Gamma')$ (`hNle`) whose restriction to $\rho(\Gamma)$ is normal (`hNnorm`) and whose relative index in $\rho(\Gamma')$ is nonzero (`hNidx`); and a datum `DM : MumfordTower 𝒪 π K₀ r g₁ N`, consisting of schemes $Z_n$ with proper flat structure maps $\mathrm{zb}_n$ to $\operatorname{Spec} \mathcal O/(\pi^{n+1})$, cartesian transition maps $\mathrm{zt}_n$, affine neighbourhoods of finite sets, and a functorial moduli map `DM.q` sending a Deligne datum over a $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ to a $B$-point of $Z_n$, compatible with the base, with base change, with the transitions, and invariant under pullback of Deligne data along elements of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ lying over $N$, together with its chart properties.
--
--   *The tower $X$ with its extra structure.* Schemes $X_n$ with maps $\mathrm{xb}_n$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O/(\pi^{n+1})$ and transitions $\mathrm{xt}_n$; a finite group $G_2$ acting by $a_n : G_2 \to \operatorname{Aut}(X_n)$; projections $\mathrm{pr}_{1,n} : X_n \to Z_n$ and $\mathrm{pr}_{2,n}$ to the spectrum of the quotient, modulo the $(n+1)$-st power of $\pi$, of the $\mathcal O$-algebra equaliser of $F_r \circ F_r$ with the identity (the fixed ring of $F_r^2$); a homomorphism $\theta : \Gamma \to G_2$; and $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphisms $\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}$ of those quotients.
--
--   *Compatibilities for $X$ (named, content summarised where indicated).* `hcart`: each square $(\mathrm{xt}_n, \mathrm{xb}_n, \mathrm{xb}_{n+1})$ over the closed immersion of bases is a pullback. `hproper`, `hflat`: each $\mathrm{xb}_n$ is proper and flat. `haff`: every finite subset of $X_n$ lies in an affine open. `ha_over`, `ha_xt`: the $G_2$-action is over the base and commutes with the transitions. `hX`: each $X_n$ is the fibre product of $Z_n$ and the spectrum of the $F_r^2$-fixed quotient over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O/(\pi^{n+1})$, via $\mathrm{pr}_{1,n}, \mathrm{pr}_{2,n}$. `hxb`, `hxt₁`, `hxt₂`: the structure map factors through $\mathrm{pr}_{1,n}$ and $\mathrm{zb}_n$, and the two projections are compatible with the transitions. `hθsurj`, `hθker`: $\theta$ is surjective and $\theta\gamma = 1$ exactly when $\rho(\gamma) \in N$. `hFr₂`: $\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}$ is induced by $F_r$ on the $F_r^2$-fixed subring. `ha_pr₂`: the automorphism $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ acts on $\mathrm{pr}_{2,n}$ through $\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}^{-v_{\det}(\sigma\gamma)}$. `ha_pr₁`: for $\gamma \in \Gamma$, a $\pi^{n+1}$-torsion $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ and Deligne data $P, P'$ over $B$ with $P'$ the pullback of $P$ along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$, composing a $B$-point of $X_n$ over `DM.q` of $P$ with $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ yields the point `DM.q` of $P'$.
--
--   *Quotient datum $DQ$ over $\mathcal O$.* A datum `DQ : TowerQuotientDatum 𝒪 π X xb xt G₂ a`, i.e. a tower $Y_n$ over $\mathcal O/(\pi^{n+1})$, proper and flat, with cartesian transitions, and finite surjective $G_2$-invariant maps $p_n : X_n \to Y_n$ with the cartesian and local-universal properties of a quotient; together with a moduli map $q$ taking, over a $\pi^{n+1}$-torsion $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$, a pair consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ and a Deligne datum over $B$, to a $B$-point of $Y_n$, subject to: `hqdef`, identifying $q$ with the composite of a point of $X_n$ with $p_n$ whenever that point realises the given Deligne datum through $\mathrm{pr}_{1,n}$ and the given algebra map through $\mathrm{pr}_{2,n}$; `hqover`, `hqnat`, `hqyt`, compatibility with the structure map, with base change along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps, and with the transitions $\mathrm{yt}_n$; and `hqinv`, invariance under the twisted action `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` of $\sigma\gamma$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma$, which Frobenius-twists the $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-component by $-v_{\det}(\sigma\gamma)$ and pulls the Deligne datum back along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$.
--
--   *Unramified presentation and comparison.* A datum `Pr : MumfordTower.NrPresentation 𝒪 π K₀ g₁ N DM Onr Fr X xb xt G₂ a pr₁ pr₂ E` with $E$ the image under $\theta$ of $\Gamma'$ viewed inside $\Gamma$; it provides schemes $X'_n$ with structure maps $\mathrm{xb}'_n$ to $\operatorname{Spec} O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi^{n+1})$, transitions $\mathrm{xt}'_n$ forming cartesian squares over the bases, $G_2$-actions $a'_n$, maps $\mathrm{qX}_n : X'_n \to X_n$ exhibiting $X'_n$ as the base change of $X_n$ along $\operatorname{Spec} O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi^{n+1}) \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O/(\pi^{n+1})$, and chart maps $\kappa'_{h,n}$, for $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, from the spectrum of $A_n := \bigl(\mathrm{chartERing}\ O^{\mathrm{nr}}\ \varpi\ r\bigr)/(\varpi^{n+1})$ to $X'_n$, where $\varpi$ denotes the image of $\pi$ and $\mathrm{chartERing}$ is the localisation, away from the element `edgeQuot.discr`, of the quotient of the polynomial ring in two variables over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ by the single relation `edgeRel`. Finally: a quotient datum `D' : TowerQuotientDatum Onr (algebraMap 𝒪 Onr π) Pr.X' Pr.xb' Pr.xt' G₂ Pr.a'` for this tower, maps $\mathrm{rY}_n : D'.Y_n \to DQ.Y_n$ exhibiting $D'.Y_n$ as the base change of $DQ.Y_n$ along the same map of bases (`hrY`), and the compatibilities `hrY_p` ($D'.p_n$ followed by $\mathrm{rY}_n$ equals $\mathrm{qX}_n$ followed by $DQ.p_n$) and `hrY_yt` ($D'.\mathrm{yt}_n$ followed by $\mathrm{rY}_{n+1}$ equals $\mathrm{rY}_n$ followed by $DQ.\mathrm{yt}_n$).
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and every $n \in \mathbb N$,
--   $$\kappa'_{h,n} \text{ followed by } \mathrm{xt}'_n \;=\; \operatorname{Spec}\ \text{of the reduction } A_{n+1} \to A_n \text{ followed by } \kappa'_{h,n+1},$$
--   where the reduction map is the factorisation of the quotient maps coming from the inclusion $(\varpi^{n+2}) \subseteq (\varpi^{n+1})$ inside $\mathrm{chartERing}\ O^{\mathrm{nr}}\ \varpi\ r$, so that its spectrum is the closed immersion $\operatorname{Spec} A_n \to \operatorname{Spec} A_{n+1}$. Thus the unramified chart maps at consecutive levels agree with the transition maps of the tower $X'$.
--
--   This is the transition law, at the level of the base-changed tower $X'$, for the unramified charts of a presentation of the Mumford tower attached to a cocompact discrete subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$: the charts at level $n$ and level $n+1$ agree under the closed immersion of the $\pi$-adic truncations of the edge-chart ring over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrCharts_transition`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrCharts_transition) and by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrFunctions_sections_of_inv`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrFunctions_sections_of_inv) in the construction of the descended quotient of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation.
